<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--

InoOnnxRuntime — Unreal Plugin Language (UPL) file for Android APK
packaging of the ONNX Runtime shared library.

Referenced from InoOnnxRuntime.Build.cs via
    AdditionalPropertiesForReceipt.Add("AndroidPlugin", "<this file>")

Two concerns handled here, matching the proven pattern from
InoAgentsLibrary_UPL_Android.xml (the LiteRT-LM UPL):

  1. Java-side loadLibrary: emit System.loadLibrary("onnxruntime")
     in the generated GameActivity Java so the library is loaded
     before libUnreal.so runs.

  2. APK staging: copy libonnxruntime.so from the plugin's
     Binaries/ThirdParty/InoOnnxRuntime/Android/arm64-v8a/ into the
     APK's lib/arm64-v8a/ directory so Android's dynamic linker can
     resolve libUnreal.so's DT_NEEDED(libonnxruntime.so) at process
     start.

Both are required. Empirically, Build.cs RuntimeDependencies alone does
NOT stage a .so into lib/arm64-v8a/ of the APK — explicit <copyFile>
in <resourceCopies> is what gets it there.

Path variable gotchas (lessons from InoAgentsLibrary_UPL_Android.xml):

  $S(AbsPluginDir)  — resolves to THIS MODULE's directory, i.e.
                       Plugins/InoAgents/Source/ThirdParty/InoOnnxRuntime/
                       (despite the "Plugin" in the name — that's how UE's
                       UPL engine labels it).
  $S(PluginDir)     — does NOT exist as a UPL variable; using it
                       produces an empty string and silently breaks the
                       copy. Always use $S(AbsPluginDir).
  $S(BuildDir)      — Intermediate/Android/<arch>/gradle/app/src/main/
  $S(Architecture)  — arm64-v8a, etc.

Our .so lives at
    Plugins/InoAgents/Binaries/ThirdParty/InoOnnxRuntime/Android/arm64-v8a/libonnxruntime.so
which is 3 levels up from $S(AbsPluginDir), then down through Binaries.

Docs: https://docs.unrealengine.com/en-US/Sharing/Reference/UnrealPluginLanguage/

-->
<root xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

	<!-- File trace for debugging: UE logs a line whenever this UPL is
	     processed. Useful for confirming the packager picked it up. -->
	<trace enable="true"/>

	<!--
	init: runs once per architecture. Gate the copies on architecture so
	we don't try to copy arm64-v8a binaries into a different arch's build
	dir. Matches the stock UE UPL pattern (see e.g. Engine/Source/ThirdParty/
	libGPUCounters/libGPUCounters_UPL.xml).
	-->
	<init>
		<log text="InoOnnxRuntime UPL init"/>
		<setBool result="bSupported" value="false"/>
		<isArch arch="arm64-v8a">
			<setBool result="bSupported" value="true"/>
		</isArch>
		<if condition="bSupported">
			<false>
				<log text="InoOnnxRuntime: unsupported architecture $S(Architecture), skipping ORT staging"/>
			</false>
		</if>
	</init>

	<!--
	soLoadLibrary: emit System.loadLibrary("onnxruntime") in the Java
	launcher activity so ORT is mapped into the process before
	libUnreal.so begins executing.

	Strictly speaking Android's dynamic linker will find libonnxruntime.so
	on its own via libUnreal.so's DT_NEEDED entry (because our Build.cs
	lists libonnxruntime.so in PublicAdditionalLibraries). But preloading
	via System.loadLibrary is belt-and-suspenders — it surfaces any load
	failure as a catchable UnsatisfiedLinkError in Java rather than a
	process-killing SIGABRT from the dynamic linker, which is a markedly
	better diagnostic experience.

	failmsg surfaces in logcat as
	    "AndroidJNI failed to load library 'onnxruntime'. Reason: <failmsg>"
	so keep it short and actionable.
	-->
	<soLoadLibrary>
		<loadLibrary name="onnxruntime" failmsg="Failed to load libonnxruntime.so — ensure OnnxRuntime/scripts/setup-onnxruntime.ps1 has been run and the APK re-packaged."/>
	</soLoadLibrary>

	<!--
	resourceCopies: copy libonnxruntime.so into the APK's
	lib/arm64-v8a/ directory. Without this, libUnreal.so's
	DT_NEEDED(libonnxruntime.so) fails to resolve at process start
	and the app crashes before any Java / UE code runs. See the
	LiteRT-LM disabled-then-re-enabled debugging history (commits
	ed733d0 through 7435e0a) for the full diagnosis of this class
	of failure.
	-->
	<resourceCopies>
		<if condition="bSupported">
			<true>
				<copyFile
					src="$S(AbsPluginDir)/../../../Binaries/ThirdParty/InoOnnxRuntime/Android/$S(Architecture)/libonnxruntime.so"
					dst="$S(BuildDir)/libs/$S(Architecture)/libonnxruntime.so"/>
				<log text="InoOnnxRuntime: copied libonnxruntime.so"/>
			</true>
		</if>
	</resourceCopies>

</root>
